.TH "UPTERM" "1" "Oct 2026" "Upterm 0.0.0+dev" "Upterm Manual"

.SH NAME
upterm-config-view - View the config file contents


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBupterm config view [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the config file, or an example config when there is none.

.PP
Config file: /home/user/.config/upterm/config.yaml

.PP
\&'upterm config edit' creates the file from the example, and checks it.

.PP
Exit status: 0, or 1 on failure.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for view


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging (log file: /home/user/.local/state/upterm/upterm.log). A non-empty DEBUG turns it on too.


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Print the config file, or the example:
  upterm config view

  # Keep a copy of it:
  upterm config view > upterm-config.yaml
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBupterm-config(1)\fP


